WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.252
A file. A domain. An address. On their

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:06.504
own, they are fragments. Pivotglass helps you follow the thread

00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:09.756
between them. This is a synthetic, offline case:

00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:13.008
the relationships are already stored, so we can explore without
pretending

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:16.260
to query a live intelligence service. Start with invoice viewer

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.512
dot bin. Its recorded relationship points to beacon check dot

00:00:19.512 --> 00:00:22.764
example. Open the domain and inspect the basis. That

00:00:22.764 --> 00:00:26.016
first pivot changes the question: what infrastructure did the file

00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:29.268
touch, and when was the connection observed? From the domain,

00:00:29.268 --> 00:00:32.520
follow resolves to the address, then hosts to the URL.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.772
Each edge has a type. Open details at each stop

00:00:35.772 --> 00:00:39.024
instead of treating a line as proof. Now a single file

00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:42.276
has led us to an infrastructure neighborhood and a more specific
collection

00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:45.528
plan. Provenance tells you where the records came from. The
chronological

00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:48.780
trail records how material entered the investigation. These are

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:52.033
reviewable paths, not an automatically reconstructed attack chain.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.894
A missing event remains missing.

00:00:54.894 --> 00:00:58.537
Two admitted indicators also share an analyst promotion group. The

00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:01.789
dotted edges preserve why we selected them together. That is

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:05.041
workflow context, not evidence of one owner. Read the

00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:08.293
complete wrapped URL, filter the neighborhood, and keep the

00:01:08.293 --> 00:01:11.545
distinctions visible. The useful result is a better test. Does this

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:14.797
topology fit common control, shared hosting, or both?

00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:18.049
Record a rationale, identify independent evidence that could

00:01:18.049 --> 00:01:21.301
separate them, and choose the next authorized collection.

00:01:21.301 --> 00:01:24.098
Pivotglass turns a connection into a question you can investigate.
